think Standfast first: swept crux/REDS.md -- every living row (80-87) is CLOSED, Released, or the custody-gated errata #75. No agent-closable red open, so the corrective queue is clear and the constructive lap may open.
think The card named the next crux-first agent-doable rung: a per-object degree read over the scene graph's overlap adjacency. It composes cleanly over scene_graph's precomputed Relation matrix (each cell carries boxes_overlap), leans on no new module, and closes with a GREEN witness -- Lindy (a relational scene primitive read for years), crux (the hardest-solvable move that opens per-region layout reads).
think Chose the crux to prove two shapes: (1) the box-overlap graph is a STAR never a clique -- a big bracket-L hub framing two dots overlaps both (degree 2) yet the two dots' boxes are disjoint, so box overlap is not transitive and degree is a LOCAL count; the hub overlaps all yet object_relation proves it 2+ pixels from each, the high-degree object the loneliest. (2) The degree is SYMMETRIC (a overlaps b iff b overlaps a, an undirected graph), the sharp contrast to scene_graph's DIRECTED nearest_neighbor over the same matrix.
obs First metal run went RED at NearestNeighborFalselySymmetric -- my directedness fixture was wrong: in this scene the far dot and hub are MUTUAL nearest neighbors, no asymmetry to show. Measurement beat memory. The real crux is box-overlap symmetry (proven here across every pair); the directed contrast is scene_graph's own proven fact, so I dropped the bad sub-fixture, replaced it with a positive full-matrix symmetry check, and reworded the claim to point at scene_graph honestly rather than over-claim. No red booked -- a design miscalc caught before GREEN, not a wrong thing shipped.
obs Caught a would-be future stamp before it landed: I pre-wrote the version const 004131, past the live clock 003915 -- exactly REDS #75's lesson the last lap flagged. Repointed the version to the live clock read at build time.
obs GREEN on the second full metal run. TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0, both new files plain 7-bit ASCII, living-card ASCII GREEN. Witness reads native `contains` (REDS #85 template), never a shell grep.
